      10["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Pobyt Service (Visit + Faraway)</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: TypeScript, NestJS]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Board frames Visit + Faraway:<br />check-in, checkout,<br />replacement room, room<br />complaints; keeps its own<br />copy of today's arrivals and<br />room status (events from<br />Rezerwacje) and builds the<br />reception emergency list from<br />it every 15 min (file +<br />e-mail); smart-lock adapter:<br />lock-to-room mapping, issues<br />and revokes mobile keys<br />(guest: check-in to checkout;<br />housekeeper: assigned room,<br />for the task).</div>"]
      style 10 fill:#438dd5,stroke:#2e6295,color:#ffffff
      11["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Synchronizacja Service (legacy ACL)</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: TypeScript, NestJS]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Board frame Synchronizacja:<br />the only place that swaps<br />files with legacy, both ways<br />every 15 min. In: room pool<br />we may sell, prices, non-pool<br />bookings, check-ins and<br />check-outs. Out: our pool<br />bookings with guest data,<br />check-ins / outs, payment<br />pre-authorisation number.<br />Numbered files, idempotent<br />import, alert on a missing<br />file; nightly full comparison<br />(pool: we win, non-pool:<br />legacy wins).</div>"]
      style 11 fill:#438dd5,stroke:#2e6295,color:#ffffff
      5["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Guest Web App</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: TypeScript, React PWA]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Room photos and descriptions,<br />availability; books a room<br />type or a specific room;<br />sends the guest to the<br />payment operator's page.</div>"]
      style 5 fill:#438dd5,stroke:#2e6295,color:#ffffff
      6["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Staff Back-office</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: TypeScript, React SPA]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Phone and walk-in bookings on<br />the same path as guests<br />(phone: the guest gets a<br />payment link), check-in /<br />out, room board, cart queue<br />panel.</div>"]
      style 6 fill:#438dd5,stroke:#2e6295,color:#ffffff
      8["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Rezerwacje Service</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: TypeScript, NestJS]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Board frame Rezerwacja + room<br />availability and status: the<br />only place that can take a<br />room for a night (one<br />transaction); holds the room<br />10 min while the guest<br />pre-authorises the payment at<br />the payment operator,<br />confirmed by webhook; never<br />waits for legacy; computes<br />when every hotel room is<br />needed next.</div>"]
      style 8 fill:#438dd5,stroke:#2e6295,color:#ffffff
      9["<div style='font-weight: bold'>Housekeeping Service</div><div style='font-size: 70%; margin-top: 0px'>[Container: TypeScript, NestJS]</div><div style='font-size: 80%; margin-top:10px'>Board frames Housekeeping +<br />Servis tech: one queue for<br />cleaning and repairs,<br />priority from when the room<br />is needed next; API for cart<br />devices. Keeps its own copy<br />of room status and room<br />needed-by (events from<br />Rezerwacje), so it works on<br />the last known state while<br />Rezerwacje is down.</div>"]
      style 9 fill:#438dd5,stroke:#2e6295,color:#ffffff
